# packaging profile (drafts D-3, D-7; assumptions A-3, A-4, A-14): Ubuntu
# packaging work on top of the orange-dev-tools SDK.
#
# SDK order (excluding the implicit system SDK): opencode, openchamber,
# gh-cli, uv, orange-dev-tools, project-packaging-tools. orange-dev-tools
# (freyes namespace, latest/edge - A-3) lands through the extra_sdks data
# loop in the shared sdks-chain partial, fed by profiles/packaging/
# vars.json, BEFORE the in-project tools SDK: hook ordering follows the
# listing order, so orange's apt packages and squid apt proxy are in place
# when the packaging-tools setup-base runs.
#
# No `runtime:` key: the default lxd-container runtime stays (A-4), so the
# snapd-dependent tooling orange's README marks best-effort is out of scope
# by design. OpenPGP signing of source uploads stays a host-side
# responsibility; nothing here forwards signing agents into the container
# (A-14).
